#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:226
msgid "Logger level configuration: programmatically"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:228
msgid ""
"After 10 iterations the level of the logger will be set to ``DEBUG``, which "
"will cause additional messages to be logged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:230
msgid ""
"Some of these debug messages cause additional functions/expressions to be "
"evaluated, which were previously skipped as ``DEBUG`` log calls were not "
"enabled. See `the source code <https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/"
"logging_demo/src/logger_usage_component.cpp>`__ of the demo for further "
"explanation of the calls used, and see the rclcpp logging documentation for "
"a full list of supported logging calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:234
msgid "Logger level configuration: externally"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:236
msgid ""
"ROS 2 nodes have services available to configure the logging level "
"externally at runtime. These services are disabled by default. The following "
"code shows how to enable the logger service while creating the node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:244
msgid ""
"// Create a node with logger service enabled\n"
"auto node = std::make_shared<rclcpp::Node>(\"NodeWithLoggerService\", "
"rclcpp::NodeOptions().enable_logger_service(true));"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:251
msgid ""
"# Create a node with logger service enabled\n"
"node = Node('NodeWithLoggerService', enable_logger_service=True)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:256
msgid ""
"If you run one of the nodes as configured above, you will find 2 services "
"when running ``ros2 service list``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:258
msgid ""
"$ ros2 service list\n"
"...\n"
"/NodeWithLoggerService/get_logger_levels\n"
"/NodeWithLoggerService/set_logger_levels\n"
"..."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:266
msgid "get_logger_levels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:268
msgid "Use this service to get logger levels for specified logger names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:270
msgid ""
"Run ``ros2 service call`` to get logger levels for ``NodeWithLoggerService`` "
"and ``rcl``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:272
msgid ""
"$ ros2 service call /NodeWithLoggerService/get_logger_levels rcl_interfaces/"
"srv/GetLoggerLevels '{names: [\"NodeWithLoggerService\", \"rcl\"]}'\n"
"\n"
"requester: making request: rcl_interfaces.srv."
"GetLoggerLevels_Request(names=['NodeWithLoggerService', 'rcl'])\n"
"\n"
"response:\n"
"rcl_interfaces.srv.GetLoggerLevels_Response(levels=[rcl_interfaces.msg."
"LoggerLevel(name='NodeWithLoggerService', level=0), rcl_interfaces.msg."
"LoggerLevel(name='rcl', level=0)])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:281
msgid "set_logger_levels"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:283
msgid "Use this service to set logger levels for specified logger names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:285
msgid ""
"Run ``ros2 service call`` to set logger levels for ``NodeWithLoggerService`` "
"and ``rcl``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:287
msgid ""
"$ ros2 service call /NodeWithLoggerService/set_logger_levels rcl_interfaces/"
"srv/SetLoggerLevels '{levels: [{name: \"NodeWithLoggerService\", level: 20}, "
"{name: \"rcl\", level: 10}]}'\n"
"\n"
"requester: making request: rcl_interfaces.srv."
"SetLoggerLevels_Request(levels=[rcl_interfaces.msg."
"LoggerLevel(name='NodeWithLoggerService', level=20), rcl_interfaces.msg."
"LoggerLevel(name='rcl', level=10)])\n"
"\n"
"response:\n"
"rcl_interfaces.srv.SetLoggerLevels_Response(results=[rcl_interfaces.msg."
"SetLoggerLevelsResult(successful=True, reason=''), rcl_interfaces.msg."
"SetLoggerLevelsResult(successful=True, reason='')])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:297
msgid ""
"There is also demo code showing how to set or get the logger level via the "
"logger service."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:299
msgid ""
"rclcpp: `demo code <https://github.com/ros2/demos/tree/rolling/"
"demo_nodes_cpp/src/logging/use_logger_service.cpp>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:301
msgid "$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp use_logger_service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:305
msgid ""
"rclpy: `demo code <https://github.com/ros2/demos/tree/rolling/demo_nodes_py/"
"demo_nodes_py/logging/use_logger_service.py>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:307
msgid "$ ros2 run demo_nodes_py use_logger_service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:313
msgid ""
"Currently, there is a limitation that ``get_logger_levels`` and "
"``set_logger_levels`` services are not thread-safe. This means that you need "
"to ensure that only one thread is calling the services at a time. Please see "
"the details in https://github.com/ros2/rcutils/issues/397"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:318
msgid "Using the logger config component"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:320
msgid ""
"The server that responds to the logger configuration requests has been "
"developed as a component so that it may be added to an existing composition-"
"based system. For example, if you are using `a container to run your nodes "
"<../../ROS-Framework/nodes/About-Composition>`, to be able to configure your "
"loggers you only need to request that it additionally load the "
"``logging_demo::LoggerConfig`` component into the container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:323
msgid ""
"As an example, if you want to debug the ``composition::Talker`` demo, you "
"can start the talker as normal with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:325
msgid "Shell 1:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:327
msgid "$ ros2 run rclcpp_components component_container"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:331
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:348
msgid "Shell 2:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:333
msgid "$ ros2 component load /ComponentManager composition composition::Talker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:337
msgid ""
"And then when you want to enable debug logging, load the ``LoggerConfig`` "
"component with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:339
msgid "Shell 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:341
msgid ""
"$ ros2 component load /ComponentManager logging_demo logging_demo::"
"LoggerConfig"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:345
msgid ""
"And finally, configure all unset loggers to the debug severity by addressing "
"the empty-named logger. Note that loggers that have been specifically "
"configured to use a particular severity will not be affected by this call."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:350
msgid ""
"$ ros2 service call /config_logger logging_demo/srv/ConfigLogger "
"\"{logger_name: '', level: DEBUG}\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:354
msgid ""
"You should see debug output from any previously unset loggers in the process "
"start to appear, including from the ROS 2 core."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:357
msgid "Logger level configuration: command line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:359
msgid ""
"As of the Bouncy ROS 2 release, the severity level for loggers that have not "
"had their severity set explicitly can be configured from the command line. "
"Restart the demo including the following command line argument:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:363
msgid "$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main --ros-args --log-level debug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:367
msgid ""
"This configures the default severity for any unset logger to the debug "
"severity level. You should see debug output from loggers from the demo "
"itself and from the ROS 2 core."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:370
msgid ""
"The severity level for individual loggers can be configured from the command-"
"line. Restart the demo including the following command line arguments:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:373
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main --ros-args --log-level "
"logger_usage_demo:=debug"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:379
msgid "Console output formatting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:381
msgid ""
"If you would like more or less verbose formatting, you can use the "
"``RCUTILS_CONSOLE_OUTPUT_FORMAT`` environment variable. For example, to "
"additionally get the timestamp and location of the log calls, stop the demo "
"and restart it with the environment variable set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:388
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:395
msgid ""
"$ export RCUTILS_CONSOLE_OUTPUT_FORMAT=\"[{severity} {time}] [{name}]: "
"{message} ({function_name}() at {file_name}:{line_number})\"\n"
"$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:402
msgid ""
"$ set \"RCUTILS_CONSOLE_OUTPUT_FORMAT=[{severity} {time}] [{name}]: "
"{message} ({function_name}() at {file_name}:{line_number})\"\n"
"$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:407
msgid ""
"You should see the timestamp in seconds and the function name, filename and "
"line number additionally printed with each message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:409
msgid ""
"For more information on configuring the console logger formatting, see the :"
"ref:`logger console configuration <logging-configuration-environment-"
"variables>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:412
msgid "Console output colorizing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:414
msgid ""
"By default, the output is colorized when it's targeting a terminal. If you "
"would like to force enabling or disabling it, you can use the "
"``RCUTILS_COLORIZED_OUTPUT`` environment variable. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:422
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:429
msgid ""
"$ export RCUTILS_COLORIZED_OUTPUT=0  # 1 for forcing it\n"
"$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:436
msgid ""
"$ set \"RCUTILS_COLORIZED_OUTPUT=0\" :: 1 for forcing it\n"
"$ ros2 run logging_demo logging_demo_main"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:441
msgid ""
"You should see that debug, warn, error and fatal logs aren't colorized now."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:445
msgid ""
"In Linux and MacOS forcing colorized output means that if you redirect the "
"output to a file, the ansi escape color codes will appear on it. In windows "
"the colorization method relies on console APIs. If it is forced you will get "
"a new warning saying that colorization failed. The default behavior already "
"checks if the output is a console or not, so forcing colorization is not "
"recommended."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:452
msgid ""
"If you start several nodes via ``ros2 launch``, no node has an active "
"terminal attached to it (unless you set ``emulate_tty=True``). This means "
"that to get colorized output for ``ros2 launch``, you need to set "
"``RCUTILS_COLORIZED_OUTPUT=1`` explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:456
msgid "Default stream for console output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:458
msgid ""
"In Foxy and later, the output from all debug levels goes to stderr by "
"default. It is possible to force all output to go to stdout by setting the "
"``RCUTILS_LOGGING_USE_STDOUT`` environment variable to ``1``. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:466
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:472
msgid "$ export RCUTILS_LOGGING_USE_STDOUT=1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:478
msgid "$ set \"RCUTILS_LOGGING_USE_STDOUT=1\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:484
msgid "Line buffered console output"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:487
msgid ""
"By default, all logging output is unbuffered. You can force it to be "
"buffered by setting the ``RCUTILS_LOGGING_BUFFERED_STREAM`` environment "
"variable to 1. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:495
#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:501
msgid "$ export RCUTILS_LOGGING_BUFFERED_STREAM=1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:507
msgid "$ set \"RCUTILS_LOGGING_BUFFERED_STREAM=1\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:511
msgid "Then run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:518
msgid "Setting the log file name prefix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:520
msgid ""
"By default, the log file name is based on the executable file name followed "
"by process ID and system timestamp on file creation. You can change the log "
"file name prefix to one of your choice using the ``--log-file-name`` command "
"line argument:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:523
msgid "$ ros2 run demo_nodes_cpp talker --ros-args --log-file-name filename"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Introspection-and-analysis/Logging-and-logger-configuration.rst:527
msgid ""
"This configures the log file name prefix to ``filename``, instead of the "
"executable file name (which is ``talker`` in this case)."
msgstr ""
